<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no">
    <meta name="description" content="Learn how <%= business.name %> collects, uses, shares, and protects information provided through its website and services.">
    <title>Privacy Policy | <%= business.name %></title>
    <link rel="shortcut icon" type="image/png" href="/images/img/favicon.png">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com/" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&amp;display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/slicknav.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/all.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/custom.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/content-pages.css" rel="stylesheet">
<link href="/css/brand.css" rel="stylesheet">
<%- include('../partials/chat') %>
<link href="/css/zoom.css" rel="stylesheet">
</head>
<body>
    <%- include('../partials/site-header') %>
    <div class="page-header"><div class="container"><div class="page-header-box"><h2>Privacy Policy</h2><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol class="breadcrumb"><li><a href="index.html">Home</a></li><li>Privacy Policy</li></ol></nav></div></div></div>

    <main class="content-page">
        <div class="container">
            <section class="content-intro">
                <div class="content-kicker">Your information</div>
                <h1>Privacy, explained clearly</h1>
                <p>This policy explains how <%= business.name %> handles information collected when you browse our website, request a quote, contact us, or use our pet transport services, including how we use, share, and protect it.</p>
            </section>

            <div class="legal-layout">
                <article class="legal-document">
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>1. Information we collect</h2><p>Information you give us may include your name, company, email, phone number, your pet's details and health information you choose to share, travel origin and destination, pickup and delivery instructions, and documents required to plan or coordinate your pet's journey.</p><p>We may also record basic website-use information, including your browser and device type, visited pages, referral source, approximate region, and access date and time.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>2. How we use information</h2><p>We use relevant information for the following purposes:</p><ul><li>Answering questions and responding to quote and service requests.</li><li>Reviewing routes, schedules, veterinary paperwork, airline rules and destination requirements.</li><li>Arranging your pet's travel with drivers, airlines, veterinarians, government agencies and destination partners.</li><li>Sending booking updates, supporting tracking, billing, and answering your questions.</li><li>Keeping the website secure, preventing misuse, and improving our service.</li><li>Fulfilling legal, regulatory, animal-health, security, and recordkeeping duties.</li></ul></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>3. Legal reasons for processing</h2><p>Our reasons for processing information depend on the service location and applicable law. They may include taking requested steps before a contract, fulfilling a contract, meeting legal duties, protecting legitimate business interests, or relying on consent where required.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>4. When information may be shared</h2><p>We share information only to the extent reasonably necessary with drivers, airlines, veterinarians, animal-health and border authorities, payment or technology providers, insurers, professional advisers, and destination partners involved in your pet's journey. Disclosure may also be required by law, a court order, or a competent authority.</p><p>Personal information is not sold by us.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>5. International transfers</h2><p>International pet relocations may require information to be transferred to, or accessed from, the United States, Australia, the United Kingdom, New Zealand, or other countries on the route. Where required, we apply reasonable contractual, organizational, or legal safeguards to these transfers.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>6. Cookies and website tools</h2><p>Cookies and similar technologies may support website operation, security, preferences, analytics, tracking, or customer support. You can restrict cookies through your browser settings, though this may affect how some features work.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>7. Retention and security</h2><p>We keep information only as long as reasonably needed for its original purpose, contractual and operational records, disputes, or legal duties. We use appropriate administrative and technical safeguards, although no online transmission or storage system is completely secure.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>8. Your choices and rights</h2><p>Your location may give you rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, object to, or transfer your information, or withdraw consent. We may still need to retain some information to meet a legal duty or an active service requirement.</p><p>To make a request, contact <a href="mailto:<%= business.email %>"><%= business.email %></a>. Identity verification may be required before we complete your request.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>9. Children’s information</h2><p>Our pet transport services are not intended for children. We do not knowingly collect children’s personal information through this website without appropriate authorization.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>10. Updates to this policy</h2><p>Changes to our services, systems, or legal requirements may lead us to update this policy. We will publish the current version and its effective date on this page.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>11. Contact us</h2><p>For questions about privacy or how we handle personal information, contact <a href="mailto:<%= business.email %>"><%= business.email %></a>.</p></section>
                </article>
                <aside class="legal-aside"><h2>Policy details</h2><p><strong>Effective date</strong><br>20 July 2026</p><p>This policy covers website visitors, customers, people receiving a pet at the destination, and people making service enquiries.</p><p><a href="terms-of-service.html">Read our Terms of Service</a></p></aside>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>

    <%- include('../partials/site-footer') %>
    
    <script src="/js/jquery-3.7.1.min.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/bootstrap.min.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/jquery.slicknav.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/service-navigation.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
